  "cli_result_text": "Submitted the file list required for the dependency-graph analysis of the Log4j2 \u2194 Spring Boot logging bridge:\n\n**Spring Boot side (detection/auto-config logic):**\n- `Log4J2LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 the `Factory` inner class gates activation on presence of `org.apache.logging.log4j.core.impl.Log4jContextFactory` (log4j-core), not the bridge modules\n- `LoggingSystem.java` \u2014 `get(ClassLoader)` entry point, `SYSTEM_PROPERTY` override\n- `LoggingSystemFactory.java` \u2014 `fromSpringFactories()` / `SpringFactoriesLoader` discovery mechanism\n- `META-INF/spring.factories` \u2014 registers `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory`\n- `spring-boot-dependencies/build.gradle` and `howto/logging.adoc` \u2014 version constraints and starter-swap guidance\n\n**Log4j2 side (bridge modules / provider SPI):**\n- `log4j-to-slf4j/pom.xml`, `SLF4JProvider.java`, `SLF4JLoggerContextFactory.java` \u2014 the API\u2192SLF4J bridge and its `Provider` SPI registration (priority 15)\n- `log4j-api/spi/Provider.java`, `util/ProviderUtil.java`, `LogManager.java` \u2014 the `META-INF/log4j-provider.properties` provider-discovery mechanism that bridge modules plug into\n- `log4j-spring-boot/Log4j2SpringBootLoggingSystem.java` \u2014 Log4j2's own `LoggingSystemFactory` override (from its Spring Cloud Config module), which competes with Spring Boot's own `Log4J2LoggingSystem.Factory` for `@Order` precedence\n- `log4j-slf4j-impl/Log4jLoggerFactory.java` \u2014 the mutual-exclusion guard against `log4j-to-slf4j` (SLF4J\u2192Log4j2 direction, opposite bridge)\n- `log4j-slf4j2-impl/pom.xml`, `log4j-bom/pom.xml` \u2014 the slf4j2-impl variant and BOM-level version alignment across bridge artifacts",
